>> title: Dukkah
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: egyptian, hazelnut, sesame, spice blend, oven
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: duqqa, duqqah, dukka
>> pairs-with: hummus, pita-bread
>> servings: 12
>> time: 30 min
>> slack: narrow — hazelnuts go from fragrant to acrid in about a minute at 350°F, and ground in there is no separating them out

Heat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C).

>> step: toast at 350°F 12 min, rub off the skins
Toast @hazelnuts{3/4%cup}(100 g) on a #baking sheet{} at 350°F for ~{12%min}, then rub off the skins in a towel.

>> step: toast in a dry skillet 2 min
Toast @coriander seeds{2%Tbs}, @cumin seeds{1%Tbs}, and @fennel seeds{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat until fragrant, about ~{2%min}.

>> step: add, toast 2 min more
Add @sesame seeds{1/2%cup}(70 g) to @&(~1)toasted spices{} and toast until golden, about ~{2%min} more.

>> step: pulse coarse in a food processor
Pulse @&(~3)hazelnuts{} with @&(~1)seeds{}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} to a coarse crumb in a #food processor{}.
